<article class="env-remark" id="08RG">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/08RG">Remark <span data-tag="08RG">92.12.5</span>.</a> In the situation of Theorem <a href="/tag/08RF" data-tag="08RF">92.12.4</a> let $I = \mathop{\mathrm{Ker}}(A \to B)$. Then $H^{-1}(L_{B/A}) = H_1(\mathcal{C}_{B/A}, \Omega ) = I/I^2$, see Lemma <a href="/tag/08RA" data-tag="08RA">92.11.2</a>. Hence $H_ k(\mathcal{C}_{B/A}, \text{Sym}^ k(\Omega )) = \wedge ^ k_ B(I/I^2)$ by Remark <a href="/tag/08SG" data-tag="08SG">92.12.2</a>. Thus the $E_1$-page looks like </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \begin{matrix}  B 

\\  0 

\\  0 

&  I/I^2 

\\  0 

&  H^{-2}(L_{B/A}) 

\\  0 

&  H^{-3}(L_{B/A}) 

&  \wedge ^2(I/I^2) 

\\  0 

&  H^{-4}(L_{B/A}) 

&  H_3(\mathcal{C}_{B/A}, \text{Sym}^2(\Omega )) 

\\  0 

&  H^{-5}(L_{B/A}) 

&  H_4(\mathcal{C}_{B/A}, \text{Sym}^2(\Omega )) 

&  \wedge ^3(I/I^2) 

\end{matrix}  \]
</div>
  <p> with horizontal differential. Thus we obtain edge maps $\text{Tor}_ i^ A(B, B) \to H^{-i}(L_{B/A})$, $i > 0$ and $\wedge ^ i_ B(I/I^2) \to \text{Tor}_ i^ A(B, B)$. Finally, we have $\text{Tor}_1^ A(B, B) = I/I^2$ and there is a five term exact sequence </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \text{Tor}_3^ A(B, B) \to H^{-3}(L_{B/A}) \to \wedge ^2_ B(I/I^2) \to \text{Tor}_2^ A(B, B) \to H^{-2}(L_{B/A}) \to 0  \]
</div>
  <p> of low degree terms. </p>
</article>